      "markdown": "---\ntitle: Finish SideStage all-seller event directory integration and audit the false-positive completion\nslug: sidestage-all-seller-event-directory-remediation-2026-08-14\nstatus: shipped\ncreated: 2026-08-14\nupdated: 2026-08-14\n---\n\n# Finish SideStage all-seller event directory integration and audit the false-positive completion\n\n## Now\n\n**State:** ⛔ PLAN CLOSED — SHIPPED 2026-08-14. Nothing in this plan is actionable. Anything below this line is the last pre-shipped snapshot, kept for history: it described work that is finished or abandoned, so do not start from it. Read frontmatter `status`, not this prose, to learn whether a plan is live (stamped by plans:set-plan-status).\n\nDraft. Plan body to be filled in.\n\n**Next:** none — the plan is shipped. (Pre-shipped next, no longer actionable: human reviews scope and lists Phase 1 items.)\n\n## Background\n\n(Why this plan exists; what problem it addresses.)\n\n## Phase 1 — TODO\n\n(Use plans:add-item to populate. Each item is one line:\nsingle id, status token, free text, optional blocked-by.)\n\n\n## Phase — Implementation and acceptance\n\n- **P-001** `done` Trace the seller principal end-to-end and inspect WI-38668/P-118's authored rubric, score writer, audit evidence, and completion verdict. importance: urgent — note: ← WI-39032 completed (done)\n- **P-002** `done` Replace hardcoded demo seller publication with the actual seller principal and display identity across event creation/update and seller-scoped reads, with regression tests. blocked-by: P-001 importance: urgent — note: ← WI-39035 completed (done)\n- **P-003** `done` Separate seeded showcase events from the normal real-data Channel Guide so real seller events are authoritative without losing explicit demo-mode support, with regression tests. blocked-by: P-001 importance: urgent — note: ← WI-39036 completed (done)\n- **P-004** `done` Run focused API/web tests, typecheck, live API/browser verification, record the corrected audit finding, and close only against an explicit end-to-end acceptance rubric. blocked-by: P-002, P-003 importance: urgent — note: ← WI-39053 completed (done)\n\n\n\n\n## Decisions\n\n(Use plans:add-decision to append. Each decision is a third-level\nheading with a date line and a body paragraph.)\n\n### D-001 — D-001 — Treat WI-38668 as a false-positive item completion, not a passed plan acceptance\nDate: 2026-08-14\nCode/ledger audit on 2026-08-14 found: (1) rubrics:search returns no rubric for the P-118 buyer Channel Guide; (2) harness_shared.plan_audits has zero rows for sidestage-standout-features-2026-08-13; (3) the parent plan remains status ready and its Now explicitly says acceptance rubric is authored after implementation, before ship; (4) WI-38668 nevertheless stored terminal completion prose beginning 'SHIPPED' after verifying eight deliberately seeded demo events, without exercising seller-created identity propagation. Therefore no rubric score was falsely marked passing—the plan-level gate was never reached. The actual failure was a work-item/plan-item false completion claim and an underspecified test oracle. Remediation acceptance must prove two independently identified sellers create events that appear together in events.guide with their own sellerId/sellerName, while explicit demo fixtures do not leak into the real-data path.\nRelated: P-001, P-002, P-003, P-004\n",
