          "id": "D-003",
          "title": "Preserve the active checkpoint, but deploy only a terminal detector-bearing verdict",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-15\nThe active Papercusp checkpoint singleton is liveness-proven by the run lock. Its SHA was initially surfaced only as candidateSource=run-probe (a cron-path checkpoint-checkout HEAD inference), so that early value was not candidate authority. The run has since published candidateSource=in-flight-candidate, authoritatively confirming it is judging 68ac9f0bdef3. That candidate predates WI-39243 detector commit e0758d0795cf: dev:pipeline_position for the detector reports judgingContainsPath=false and nextContainsPath=true. Do not duplicate, replace, or deploy the active run. After it reaches terminal, read the candidate from the verdict. If the terminal verdict does not contain e0758 plus release repairs 7b37bfc712, 0700efa08a, and 1373cead0b53, launch exactly one current-staging checkpoint; deploy only a terminal green descendant containing all four, verify direct serving-process SHA and SSE health, then resume release-trigger. SideStage public-release D-020 separately governs SideStage candidate identity and forbids substituting this Papercusp checkpoint SHA for pipeline_events.detail.candidate.",
