          "id": "D-006",
          "title": "D-005/D-024 release-snapshot freeze is SATISFIED and now OBE — all 12 items are blocked only by an unflipped status, not a live condition",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\nVerified 2026-08-17T15:0xZ by su-7c55c214 under WI-39711, on the lane the fleet leader relayed from [owner:Avi 2026-08-17, interactive] widening the mandate to whole-app submission readiness.\n\nD-005 (mirroring release-plan D-024) froze P-001..P-012 until: ec755db published by normal git-sync + a fresh authoritative SideStage verdict + exactly one serialized green deployment + fresh public seller acceptance, with residues EI-20485490544986949 and EI-20496543498783917 terminalized from that proof. Each leg, measured rather than assumed:\n\n1. ec755db PUBLISHED — CONFIRMED. `git merge-base --is-ancestor ec755db738c778758368be696d2a0685e2aba281 <ref>` returns true for origin/staging AND origin/main. The plan's ## Now still says \"the last direct remote read still had origin/staging at cf3265f9\"; that is stale — origin/staging is now 4bfc31f.\n\n2. SERIALIZED GREEN DEPLOYMENT — CONFIRMED by promotion, which is the stronger signal. origin/main == origin/staging == 4bfc31f. main only advances when the green-checkpoint gate passes, so main sitting AT 4bfc31f is itself proof the gate went green on that pin. This also retires the separate 13:15Z \"green-checkpoint NOT-GREEN on schema drift, main is frozen\" blocker (EI-20707115450160760, itself closed 14:01Z) — main is demonstrably not frozen.\n\n3. RESIDUES TERMINALIZED — CONFIRMED. EI-20485490544986949 (Copilot sync mutation rejects an owned event after seller identity switch) state=done, closedAt 2026-08-16T07:11:33.192Z. EI-20496543498783917 (public event directory empty after deployment, seller Copilot exact verification 404s) state=done, closedAt 2026-08-16T07:11:33.423Z. WI-39007/P-009, the release-promotion item the freeze hung on, state=done, closedAt 2026-08-16T07:11:32.757Z. All three closed within one second of each other on 08-16, i.e. the proof the freeze demanded landed the day after the freeze was written.\n\nCONCLUSION: the freeze condition was met on 2026-08-16 and nothing has re-armed it. The 12 items are not blocked by any live condition — they carry a stale `blocked` status that outlived its cause by a day, across two shipped plans (release-drive 08-16, WS cutover 08-17). The freeze should be lifted and the items re-baselined rather than treated as gated work.\n\nONE CAVEAT, stated so nobody reads more into this than the evidence supports: all three closes carry completionAuthority=null, meaning they were closed via the bare state-write path and never passed the work_items:complete evidence gate. Per the audit semantics that means \"never judged\", NOT \"unevidenced\" — so this decision rests on the items being TERMINAL (which D-005 is what asked for) and on the independently measured git lineage above, not on the quality of those closes. I did NOT re-verify the underlying seller-acceptance behaviour itself; the \"fresh public seller-JHGLDS acceptance\" leg is attested only by those item closures. If a stricter reading of D-024 is wanted, that behavioural leg is the one to re-run.\n\nNEXT: this decision only unblocks the lane. Which of the 12 gaps still REPRODUCE on today's tree is a separate question, being answered now by a clean-clone re-baseline under WI-39711; findings land there and as a follow-up decision.\nRelated: P-001, P-002, P-003, P-004, P-005, P-006, P-007, P-008, P-009, P-010, P-011, P-012",
