          "id": "D-007",
          "title": "Clean-clone re-baseline 2026-08-17: Phase 0 no longer reproduces — 3 items measured satisfied, 2 likely landed, 6 unassessed, 1 still real",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\nRe-baseline run by su-7c55c214 under WI-39711, following D-006 (freeze OBE). Method: genuine reviewer-path clean clone OUTSIDE the shared tree — `git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/Papercusp/sidestage.git /tmp/sidestage-rebaseline-20260817-110213`, HEAD 4bfc31f on main, all 12 submodules, then the README's own documented commands. Nothing was fixed; this lane is report-first by leader instruction.\n\nMEASURED RESULT (each command run TWICE, because P-002's acceptance is literally \"exit zero twice from a clean worktree\"):\n  npm install         exit 0\n  npm run typecheck   exit 0  /  exit 0\n  npm test            exit 0  /  exit 0   — 1,736 passed, 13 skipped, 0 failed across 4 vitest projects\n  npm run build       exit 0  /  exit 0\n  npm run dev         BOOTS — API /healthz returned {\"status\":\"ok\",\"service\":\"sidestage-api\",\"version\":\"0.1.0\"}, Vite v7.3.6 ready in 428ms serving real HTML.\n\nPER-ITEM VERDICT:\n\nSATISFIED BY MEASUREMENT (3):\n- P-002 — its exact acceptance is what I measured, twice. The baseline test/typecheck/build failures it exists to repair DO NOT REPRODUCE on today's tree.\n- P-001 — premise stale. It exists to pin a baseline and capture clean-checkout test/build/demo FAILURES as fixtures. Those failures are gone, so there is nothing left to capture. Needs re-scoping (or closing), not execution.\n- P-012 — the fresh-clone gate it specifies (setup, dev smoke, test, typecheck, build at one commit) is exactly the procedure I just executed end-to-end, and it passes. What remains of P-012 is only AUTOMATING it as a recurring gate; the underlying condition is green.\n\nLIKELY ALREADY LANDED, NOT CLAUSE-BY-CLAUSE CONFIRMED (2):\n- P-006 / P-007 — db/schema.sql now carries targeted_offer (offer_id PK, event/item/audit FKs, status constraint), action_audit_entry, policy_audit_entry, policy_idempotency, policy_outbox_event. apps/api/src/actions carries targeted-offer.store.ts (+test), action-audit.store.ts, PgActionItemStore (+test), with tests named \"PgTargetedOfferStore provenance and rollback\", \"create idempotency on the originating command\", \"creates a targeted offer, reserves its quantity, and restores it on rollback\", \"collapses a foreign audit id and an absent audit id without applying rollback\". This is plausibly the WS-cutover P-001 work (WI-39614, \"actions, offers, and audit records — durable Postgres authority\") landing the same scope. I did NOT check each acceptance clause; someone should before closing them.\n\nSTILL LIKELY REAL (1):\n- P-010 — \"make npm run dev supply the documented sunday-drop event\". `npm run dev` boots, and sunday-drop appears throughout code and tests, and db/seed/demo.sql exists — but README's Quick start never instructs a reviewer to seed anything, and the seed path needs Postgres via docker compose. So a reviewer following the README verbatim very likely gets a running app with NO demo event. I did not run the docker path, so this is a strong indication rather than a reproduction.\n\nNOT ASSESSED — no evidence gathered either way (6): P-003, P-004, P-005 (claim/evidence contract, reply-guard binding, adversarial fixtures), P-008, P-009 (requiredProperties/fallback, latency benchmark), P-011 (doc reconciliation). These are behavioural/product-surface items that a green build says nothing about. Do not read this decision as clearing them.\n\nMETHOD CAVEATS, stated so this is re-checkable rather than trusted:\n1. Ports. The documented defaults 3100/5173 are OCCUPIED by live services on this host, so I used the README's own WEB_PORT/API_PORT override (3399/5399). The default-port experience on a clean reviewer machine is therefore NOT verified by me.\n2. The suite ran without docker compose; PG-integration tests self-skip (13 skipped). A reviewer running the documented commands gets the same, so this matches the reviewer path — but it is not full coverage.\n3. Green build/test/typecheck says nothing about product correctness, which is exactly why the six items above are marked unassessed rather than passed.\n\nSEPARATE DEFECT FOUND, filed as WI-39713: the public repo tracks 17 `.papercup-console-active.<pid>` agent scratch files at its ROOT, reproduced in the clean clone — the first thing a contest evaluator sees. Fix shape is `git rm --cached` plus a `.gitignore` rule; the ignore rule is the load-bearing half, since an automatic whole-tree sync put them there and will do so again.\n\nRECOMMENDATION: unfreeze the plan, close/re-scope P-001+P-002+P-012 against this evidence, verify P-006/P-007 against their acceptance clauses, and re-point the remaining effort at P-003/P-004/P-005/P-008/P-009/P-010/P-011 — the items a green gate cannot speak to.\nRelated: P-001, P-002, P-003, P-004, P-005, P-006, P-007, P-008, P-009, P-010, P-011, P-012",
