          "title": "Papercusp release-trigger hold protects the repair-bearing cutover",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-15\nThe Papercusp release-trigger pause remains mandatory until its owner announces verified repair-bearing live proof. Do not deploy green pin 1feac8dd867c and do not re-enable release-trigger: that pin predates the release-checkout and queued-fire repairs. Singleton checkpoint 961fe6e0 is still active and CPU-advancing but is itself pre-repair; its owner will launch exactly one fresh repair-bearing checkpoint after it reaches terminal. A peer manual trigger already produced an unsafe partial state (release checkout/ledger moved to 1fe while the process still served 962), which the hold owner is restoring. Source authority: peer disposition msu7oarz-0000-e9f1a7614b1548fc869dfe270aab49da; acknowledgement msu7pql7. SideStage D-010 stays read-only until the repair-bearing live-proof announcement, then generation/deployed/public equality must still be proven independently.\nRelated: P-009, P-014",
