      "markdown": "---\ntitle: SideStage: event lifecycle controls (schedule/go-live/end + auto-go-live) and a real homepage default event\nslug: sidestage-event-lifecycle-and-home-default-2026-08-17\nstatus: shipped\ncreated: 2026-08-17\nupdated: 2026-08-17\n---\n\n## Now\n\n**State:** ⛔ PLAN CLOSED — SHIPPED 2026-08-17. Nothing in this plan is actionable. Anything below this line is the last pre-shipped snapshot, kept for history: it described work that is finished or abandoned, so do not start from it. Read frontmatter `status`, not this prose, to learn whether a plan is live (stamped by plans:set-plan-status).\n\nP-001 first (smallest, fixes the visible homepage defect), then P-002, then the P-003 -> P-004/P-005 lifecycle chain, then P-006 verification.\n\n**Next:** none — the plan is shipped.\n\n## Background\n\nOwner report, 2026-08-17, against the deployed site sidestage.papercusp.com.\n\n**Confirmed diagnosis (read from source + the live API), all three:**\n\n1. **Homepage opens the wrong event.** `apps/web/src/event-identity.ts` hardcodes\n   `DEFAULT_EVENT_ID = 'sunday-drop'` / `DEFAULT_EVENT_TITLE = 'Sunday vintage drop'`, and\n   `App.tsx:59` seeds `activeEventId` from `browserEventId()`, which falls back to that\n   constant whenever the URL carries no `?event=`. The Channel Guide directory is never\n   consulted for the default. Live evidence: `GET https://sidestage.papercusp.com/api/events`\n   returns exactly one row — `avi-real-test` (\"Avi Real Test\", status `scheduled`,\n   `startsAt: null`) — so production's homepage opens a room that does not exist in the\n   directory at all, while the sidebar's topmost row is Avi Real Test. Compounding it,\n   `EventService.listForGuide()` filters out `isSyntheticSellerIdentity` rows and the seeded\n   `sunday-drop` is owned by `demo-seller`, so even on the demo path the pinned default is\n   excluded from the very sidebar it is supposed to match.\n\n2. **No lifecycle control exists — it is missing, not hidden.** The `event` table already\n   carries `status` (CHECK draft|scheduled|live|ended), `starts_at` and `ended_at`, and the\n   guide reads all three (`compareForGuide`, `formatStartLabel` countdown). But the only\n   event mutations in the API are `PUT /events/:eventId/config` (publishes draft -> scheduled\n   via `EventService.publishFromConfig`) and `DELETE /events/:eventId` (unpublish -> draft).\n   Nothing anywhere writes `status='live'`, `status='ended'`, or `starts_at`. Verified by grep\n   across `apps/api/src`: no `@Patch`/`@Post` on the events controllers, and the only `'live'`\n   literals are demo seed rows and sort-rank helpers. The existing `DELETE` also has no UI.\n\n3. **Settings preflight section.** `EventReadinessPanel.tsx` renders the eyebrow\n   \"Current event · preflight\" + `<h2>Event readiness</h2>`; it is mounted at exactly one call\n   site, `ConfigTab.tsx:333`, inside `EventSettingsPanel` (the Event Manager > Settings\n   section). The shared preflight types/helpers in `rehearsals.ts` are ALSO used by the Tests\n   tab, so they stay; only the panel, its call site, its test and its dead `.event-readiness-*`\n   CSS go.\n\n## Decisions\n\n### D-001 The homepage default event is derived from the guide, never a constant\n\n`browserEventId()`'s `?event=` deep-link seeding is preserved so existing share links keep\nresolving. When the URL names no event, the active event follows the Channel Guide's FIRST\nrow — the same order the sidebar paints (`compareForGuide`: live-by-viewers, then\nsoonest-scheduled, then most-recently-ended). The hardcoded `sunday-drop` fallback is removed\nrather than repointed: any constant here is a second source of truth that can drift out of the\ndirectory again, which is exactly the reported defect. An empty guide yields an honest empty\nstate, not a phantom room.\n\n### D-002 Lifecycle is one guarded transition endpoint, not four verbs\n\nSchedule / go-live / end are one owner-checked transition surface on the event resource rather\nthan three routes, so the legal-transition table lives in one place server-side and the UI\ncannot invent a transition the store will not honour. Unpublish keeps its existing DELETE.\n\n### D-003 Auto-go-live is a server-side sweep, never a client timer\n\n[owner:Avi 2026-08-17, chose \"Full + auto-go-live at the scheduled time\"] A `scheduled` event\nwhose `starts_at` has passed flips to `live` server-side. A browser-side flip would fire only\nfor whoever happens to have the tab open, and would be a write originating from an\nunauthenticated buyer surface. Per the repo scheduling convention this is a declared scheduled\nsweep, never a bare `setInterval`.\n\n### D-004 — Removing EventReadinessPanel supersedes the readiness-IA plan's D-008 clause that embedded it\nDate: 2026-08-17\n[owner:Avi 2026-08-17, verbatim: \"in the settings tab remove the 'Current event · preflight / Event readiness' section entirely\"]\n\nP-002 deletes `apps/web/src/EventReadinessPanel.tsx` and its single call site in `ConfigTab.tsx`'s `EventSettingsPanel`. That directly contradicts a still-standing prior ruling, so record the supersession rather than leave a future agent to \"restore\" the panel by citing it.\n\nThe prior ruling is **D-008 of plan `sidestage-event-settings-readiness-ia-2026-08-14`** (surviving verbatim in `apps/api/src/build-history/build-history.snapshot.ts`): \"legacy config URLs resolve to Studio, where EventSettingsPanel **and EventReadinessPanel** are embedded in the event-scoped Studio/Event Manager workflow.\"\n\nWhat SURVIVES of D-008: the route IA. Five top-level routes (Watch, Orders, Studio, Releases, Tests), no separate Settings route, no Rehearse label, legacy config URLs resolving into Studio, and `EventSettingsPanel` embedded in Event Manager — all unchanged by this plan.\n\nWhat is SUPERSEDED: the `EventReadinessPanel` half of that clause only. The panel is gone from the Settings section by owner instruction. Its shared preflight machinery is NOT removed — `rehearsals.ts` (`PreflightReport`, the `rehearsal.preflight` sync query, the client probes) stays, because `TestTab.tsx` reads it and the Tests route still renders synthetic suites exactly as D-008 describes. `sync-contract.test.ts` was narrowed to stop reading the deleted file while keeping its TestTab preflight assertions.\n\nRecurrence guard: `ConfigTab.test.tsx` now asserts the ABSENCE of \"Event readiness\", \"Current event · preflight\" and \"Run event preflight\" in the rendered settings form, so a future re-embed fails a test instead of silently landing. Note the adjacent \"Configuration readiness\" progressbar is a DIFFERENT surface that stays — the two read almost identically in a diff, which is why the guard names the exact strings.\n\n## Phase 1\n\n- **P-001** `done` Homepage default event follows the Channel Guide's topmost row instead of the hardcoded `sunday-drop`; `?event=` deep links still win importance: high\n- **P-002** `done` Remove the \"Current event · preflight / Event readiness\" section from the Settings tab entirely (panel + call site + test + dead CSS; keep the shared rehearsals preflight the Tests tab uses)\n- **P-003** `done` API: event lifecycle transitions — store methods (in-memory + PG) and one owner-guarded endpoint that sets a scheduled start time, takes an event live, and ends it importance: high\n- **P-004** `done` API: auto-flip `scheduled` -> `live` once `starts_at` passes, as a declared server-side sweep blocked-by: P-003\n- **P-005** `done` Web: Event Manager lifecycle controls — start date/time, Go live, End event, Unpublish — on the event detail header, invalidating the guide/directory after each write blocked-by: P-003 — note: Lifecycle controls + client legality mirror + differential test; 4 repo guards satisfied\n- **P-006** `done` Verify end-to-end against the running app (homepage default, lifecycle round-trip, settings section gone) and run the affected suites blocked-by: P-001, P-002, P-004, P-005 — note: ← WI-39673 completed (done)\n\n",
