          "title": "macOS hardware gate: xcframework/simulator/host-smoke items are NOT claimable on Linux hosts — Linux-feasible work only; build+verify items park blocked pending a Mac runner",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nThe whole fleet runs on a Linux host (marsh-office); xcodebuild/xcframework assembly and Swift host-smoke CANNOT run here. Ruling: (1) items whose acceptance requires macOS tooling (WI-38622 xcframework build + Swift-boundary smoke) sit state:blocked — NOT circulating in claim pools; the dock spec handed WI-38622 to e1a3a at 05:2xZ and was correctly refused/released. (2) Linux-FEASIBLE iphone-plan work stays claimable: shared Rust core (sidestage-core), UniFFI bindings source generation, build-script authoring, anything verifiable via cargo on Linux. Preserve D-001 (consume shared core, no duplication). (3) The macOS gap is an OWNER-GATED WALL: surfaced to Avi in the leader's status report — either a macOS runner gets attached, or iOS items terminate at source-complete + Linux-verified with the build/smoke tail parked. [self-imposed leader ruling; supplements D-005 re-open]",
