          "title": "Shipped Ticket theme tokens only — this is an IA change, not a re-skin",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\nEvery screen in the accepted mockup uses the shipped Ticket theme verbatim: `--bg #FFF8EF` cream ground, `--brand-red #D62B1F`, `--brand-yellow #FFC400`, `--text #2A1F1A`, `--muted #77685A`, `--success #196B42`, Inter. That palette was picked by Avi from the P-001 mockups ('lets go with R3') and is pinned by D-004 of the retheme.\n\nWhat changes in this plan is information architecture and interaction — order, hierarchy, disclosure, guardrail visibility — NOT colour, type, or brand. Do not introduce a new palette, a new font, or new hexes: a colour with no token gets a NEW NAMED TOKEN in styles.css (retheme D-002), never an inline hex.\n\nSupporting signal: owner memory 0f8cac06 records Avi rejecting a wholesale visual redesign on another Papercusp surface as 'ugly — I wanted unique, not ugly', preferring the existing look improved by addition. A re-skin here would be re-deciding something he has already decided.\n\nThe density tokens (`--ss-font`, `--ss-control-h`, `--ss-pad`, `--ss-gap`) already exist with a seller/console tier — use them for the target-size fix (fault 4) rather than hardcoding new sizes.",
