      "slug": "sidestage-lineup-run-of-show-mockups-2026-08-14",
      "title": "SideStage Lineup + Run of Show unified redesign mockups",
      "status": "shipped",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-15",
      "contentHash": "16786480678f5636adc27fa6d6f4029f056166e31373917893f5c6252a67f0ca",
      "markdown": "---\ntitle: SideStage Lineup + Run of Show unified redesign mockups\nslug: sidestage-lineup-run-of-show-mockups-2026-08-14\nstatus: shipped\ncreated: 2026-08-15\nupdated: 2026-08-15\n---\n\n## Goal\n\nExplore removing the separate Rehearse tab by folding draggable run-of-show authoring into a substantially improved Event Manager Lineup. Produce comparable browser-rendered concepts only; do not alter the production app.\n\n## Constraints\n\nReuse SideStage's existing design language and real event/lineup semantics. Preserve price, inventory, guarded actions, optional time budgets, talking-point notes, and advisory-only live sequencing. Include useful empty/loading/error states and mobile behavior.\n\n## Now\n\n**State:** ⛔ PLAN CLOSED — SHIPPED 2026-08-15. Nothing in this plan is actionable. Anything below this line is the last pre-shipped snapshot, kept for history: it described work that is finished or abandoned, so do not start from it. Read frontmatter `status`, not this prose, to learn whether a plan is live (stamped by plans:set-plan-status).\n\nApproved by Avi for direct execution in this session. Registry search found no matching react-tailwind entries, so use shipped SideStage components and tokens as the reuse source.\n\n**Next:** none — the plan is shipped.\n\n## Phase — Design exploration\n\n- **P-001** `done` Audit the current Lineup, run-of-show planner, shipped mockups, and SideStage visual tokens; define the shared content model for all concepts. importance: high — note: ← WI-39106 completed (done)\n- **P-002** `done` Build three interactive browser mockup directions that merge draggable run-of-show planning into a redesigned Lineup, with desktop and mobile behavior. blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: ← WI-39116 completed (done)\n- **P-003** `done` Author UI-IR specs for the concepts and run design-phase validation plus anti-pattern lint; correct every blocking issue. blocked-by: P-002 importance: high — note: ← WI-39200 completed (done)\n- **P-004** `done` Run browser visual and interaction QA across the concepts, then present a comparison and recommendation to Avi without modifying production. blocked-by: P-003 importance: high — note: ← WI-39205 completed (done)\n\n\n\n\n## Phase — Ad-hoc auction launcher\n\n- **P-005** `done` Search the design registry for SideStage-native panel, action, input, status, product-list, and drawer patterns; capture the current desktop Active Event screen as the visual reference. blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: ← WI-39115 completed (done)\n- **P-006** `done` Define three Active Event ad-hoc auction launch concepts—on-deck actions, run-of-show row actions, and a dedicated auction launcher panel—and validate/lint their UI IR. blocked-by: P-005 importance: high — note: ← WI-39121 completed (done)\n- **P-007** `done` Generate one high-fidelity SideStage visual mockup for each validated auction concept using the current Active Event capture as reference. blocked-by: P-006 importance: high — note: ← WI-39123 completed (done)\n- **P-008** `done` Compare live-operation speed, screen density, error prevention, extensibility, and mobile adaptation; present the three auction mockups and a recommendation to Avi. blocked-by: P-007 importance: high — note: ← WI-39130 completed (done)\n\n\n## Phase — Implementation\n\n- **P-009** `done` Implement Avi's approved combined Active Event design in the canonical SideStage staging tree: embed the next-product auction launcher inside RunOfShowPanel, reuse event.auction.active plus the existing auction.start command and seller credential boundary, support opening bid and duration, keep later rows compact and add no On deck panel, add focused component/integration regression coverage, then browser-verify the live flow against the accepted 1672x941 mockup. importance: high — note: ← WI-39159 completed (done)\n\n## Decisions\n\n### D-001 — Ad-hoc auction launch belongs in Active Event\nDate: 2026-08-15\nAvi ruled that seller auction launch is a live-show action, not an Event Manager setup action. Every auction mockup must expose Start auction inside Active Event. Event Manager may retain setup/history, but it cannot be the only launch path.\nRelated: P-005, P-006, P-007, P-008\n\n### D-002 — Implement auction launch as a RunOfShowPanel extension\nDate: 2026-08-15\nDate: 2026-08-15\nThe approved combined mockup is implemented by extending the shipped RunOfShowPanel and the existing auction.start/event.auction.active contracts. The next planned item owns the inline launcher; Event Manager may retain its setup/history surface, but no second On deck or auction dock panel is added. Seller credentials, active-auction exclusion, inventory authority, and server duration validation remain unchanged.\nRelated: P-009\n",
