          "id": "D-007",
          "title": "D-006's papergrid-bridge criterion is gradeable after all — it measured a canvas the app never mounts; re-checked and PASSING on production",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\nDate: 2026-08-14. Recorded by su-3b39b6c3 while re-checking the D-006 caveat for P-007 of sidestage-public-release-testing-2026-08-14 (WI-38799). This CORRECTS the framing of D-006 and unblocks its follow-up EI-20411520596913364; it does not dispute the honesty of the original grade, which was right to refuse to call an unmeasured criterion a pass.\n\nWHAT D-006 SAYS: the papergrid-bridge criterion is UNKNOWN/vacuous (0-of-0) because \"papergrid renders ZERO canvases on production\", with EI-20411520596913364 left open to \"grade the bridge against a real canvas render once production exercises papergrid\".\n\nWHY THAT UNBLOCK CAN NEVER ARRIVE (source-verified): papergrid ships TWO grids in libs/papergrid/grid-core/src/ — DataGridShell.tsx (glide-data-grid, paints to a 2D <canvas>) and RichGrid.tsx (plain DOM, emits <div role=\"row\">). apps/web imports ONLY RichGrid: event-creation/InventoryPickerGrid.tsx and events/EventLineupGrid.tsx. `grep -rn DataGridShell apps/web/src` returns NOTHING outside a comment. So \"zero canvases\" is literally TRUE and stays true — it counts a component SideStage never mounts. Waiting for production to \"exercise papergrid\" via a canvas is waiting for something the code cannot produce.\n\nTHE CRITERION WAS ALWAYS GRADEABLE, just not by counting canvases: RichGrid.tsx imports GRID_COLORS from grid-theme.ts, which is exactly the object applyGridTheme() mutates through configureGridColors() (main.tsx calls it after styles.css and before first render). The bridge's effect is therefore visible in the colours RichGrid PAINTS.\n\nFALSIFIER USED: grid-theme.ts's NEUTRAL default is dark — headerBg #0e0e0e, bg #141414, rowAlt #1a1a1a, text #e6e6e6. Those are precisely the \"black strip with near-white titles on cream\" defect the bridge was written to fix, so a probe that fails on seeing them cannot pass vacuously. Probe: apps/web/tools/theme-audit/probe-papergrid-bridge.mjs (own isolated Chromium, per EI-20403007799747278; carries the README's token control + a render proof, and exits 3 = ABSENT rather than 0 when no grid mounts).\n\nRESULT — measured 2026-08-14 14:57Z against https://sidestage.buyrestart.com (D-006's own subject), and identically against local :5173:\n  control OK (--brand-red #D62B1F, --surface-sunken #FBF2E3, undefined token \"\")\n  canvases: 0  — D-006's literal observation reproduces, and is confirmed irrelevant\n  RichGrid rows painted: 51\n  header bg #fbf2e3 == --surface-sunken EXACTLY; rows alternate #ffffff / #fff8ef; text #2a1f1a\n  NONE of #0e0e0e / #141414 / #1a1a1a / #e6e6e6 present anywhere\nVERDICT: PASS. The R3 bridge demonstrably reaches the live grid on production.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: the shipped R3 status may now be read as 6-of-6 verified rather than \"5 verified + 1 unverifiable-in-production\". EI-20411520596913364 is resolved by this evidence; its stated precondition should NOT be carried forward, because any future agent inheriting it will wait on a canvas render that cannot occur.\n\nLIVE RICHGRID MOUNT PATH, for whoever re-runs this: seller tab -> event-manager dock panel -> EventManager (loaded && pickerOpen) -> EventCreationPanel -> InventoryPickerGrid. Note EventLineupGrid is imported by NO application file (only its own test), so InventoryPickerGrid is currently the ONLY live RichGrid — if that changes, re-check both.",
