      "markdown": "---\ntitle: Extract Restart Scout backend runtime and run SideStage Scout on Vertex Gemini\nslug: sidestage-scout-shared-runtime-vertex-2026-08-14\nstatus: active\ncreated: 2026-08-14\nupdated: 2026-08-14\n---\n\n## Goal\nExtract Restart's proven backend agent loop into a reusable shared TypeScript package and make both Restart and SideStage consume it while preserving the already-shared drawer, SSE transport, and chat protocol.\n\n## Constraints\n- Vertex Gemini authenticates through existing Application Default Credentials; no credential material enters either repository.\n- Preserve Restart's working shopper behavior and wire contract.\n- Keep catalog, cart, identity, session, memory, prompt, persistence, and app-specific stream events behind application adapters.\n- Add package, unit, integration, and typecheck evidence before completion.\n\n## Now\nBuild the shared runtime first, then migrate the two applications in parallel-safe dependency order, then verify end-to-end.\n\n## Phase — Implementation\n\n- **P-001** `done` Create the standalone @papercusp/scout-runtime package with provider-neutral message/tool types, bounded agent-turn runner, retry policy, budget and telemetry hooks, a Vertex Gemini adapter using ADC, and focused unit tests. importance: urgent — note: ← WI-39039 completed (done)\n- **P-002** `done` Migrate Restart apps/scout-service to consume @papercusp/scout-runtime while retaining Restart-specific prompts, sessions, memory, persistence, catalog/cart handlers, interactive cards, and wire events. blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: ← WI-39048 completed (done)\n- **P-003** `done` Integrate SideStage apps/api Scout with @papercusp/scout-runtime and implement SideStage-specific catalog/cart tool handlers plus Vertex configuration, without changing the shared drawer/SSE/chat protocol. blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: ← WI-39071 completed (done)\n- **P-004** `done` Run package and application unit tests, affected tests, typechecks, and focused live/integration verification for natural-language catalog questions and tool calls; resolve any regressions. blocked-by: P-002, P-003 importance: urgent — note: ← WI-39081 completed (done)\n- **P-005** `todo` Verify shared-package publication/submodule pointers and both deployment configurations, record exact evidence, and close the migration plan. blocked-by: P-004\n\n## Decisions\n\n### D-001 — Keep browser and backend packages separate\nDate: 2026-08-14\n@papercusp/scout-chat remains the browser-only drawer/transport package. Backend execution belongs in a standalone @papercusp/scout-runtime package so React/browser peer dependencies never leak into server services.\n\n### D-002 — Define the runtime/application seam\nDate: 2026-08-14\nThe shared runtime owns provider-neutral message and tool types, bounded model/tool rounds, retries, usage normalization, budget and telemetry hooks, and provider adapters. Each application owns system prompts, identity/session/memory/persistence, catalog/cart and other domain handlers, and app-specific emitted events.\n\n### D-003 — Use Vertex Application Default Credentials\nDate: 2026-08-14\nThe Gemini adapter uses Google Vertex AI through the existing machine Application Default Credentials and externally supplied project/location configuration. No API key or credential file is copied or committed. SCOUT_VERTEX_MODEL remains overrideable; the initial default follows the live OMP catalog's function-calling-capable Gemini 3.1 Pro preview identifier.\n\n### D-004 — Preserve the established client wire contract\nDate: 2026-08-14\nThe existing @papercusp/scout-chat drawer, @papercusp/sse transport, and @papercusp/chat-protocol event contract remain unchanged. Migration is behind the server boundary and app adapters.\n",
