          "id": "D-021",
          "title": "Board resize width clamps to its parent column (leader default, owner may override)",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-14\n[self-imposed leader ruling 2026-08-14 — NOT owner-directed; owner Avi may override] WI-38712 (P-015 whole-board resize) closed with one undetermined reading flagged in completion residue: may the board's resizable width EXCEED its parent column width? Ruling: NO — clamp to the parent column. Rationale: an overflowing board breaks the seller-page column layout, and no owner turn requests overflow; the owner's verbatim ask (\"the full width and height of the entire board should also be resizeable\") is satisfied by resize-within-parent. If the shipped behavior differs from clamp, that delta is a follow-up work-item, not a reopen of WI-38712. Disclosed to the owner in the leader status report; an owner override supersedes this decision.\nRelated: P-015",
          "date": "2026-08-14",
