      "contentHash": "43d105d463d81909a0a9c68e144a43d2adb927f61b22dc463aaa0d64aed1d994",
      "markdown": "---\ntitle: Sidestage Studio event activation and scheduling UX mockups\nslug: sidestage-studio-event-activation-scheduling-mockups-2026-08-14\nstatus: ready\ncreated: 2026-08-15\nupdated: 2026-08-15\n---\n\n# Sidestage Studio event activation and scheduling UX mockups\n\n## Now\n\n**State:** Complete. Current-state audit, zero-warning interaction model (D-001), four project-bound mockups, validation, and owner delivery are complete; canonical P-001 through P-004 are done.\n\n**Next:** No further work in this design-only plan. Product implementation remains outside scope and behind the Sidestage P-009 release-snapshot gate.\n\n## Background\n\n(Why this plan exists; what problem it addresses.)\n\n## Phase 1 — TODO\n\n(Use plans:add-item to populate. Each item is one line:\nsingle id, status token, free text, optional blocked-by.)\n\n\n## Phase — Discovery and design\n\n- **P-001** `done` Audit the current Studio web experience and source for event activation/start controls importance: high — note: ← WI-39119 completed (done)\n- **P-002** `done` Search the shared UI registry and define the start-now, scheduling, and seller-visibility interaction model blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: ← WI-39122 completed (done)\n- **P-003** `done` Create polished visual mockups grounded in the existing Sidestage interface blocked-by: P-001, P-002 importance: high — note: ← WI-39131 completed (done)\n- **P-004** `done` Validate the mockups and deliver findings with implementation guidance blocked-by: P-003 importance: high — note: ← WI-39134 completed (done)\n- **P-005** `dropped` Audit the current Studio web experience and source for event activation/start controls importance: high — note: Duplicate entries created after multi-ptool output was not surfaced; canonical work remains P-001 through P-004.\n- **P-006** `dropped` Search the shared UI registry and define the start-now, scheduling, and seller-visibility interaction model blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: Duplicate entries created after multi-ptool output was not surfaced; canonical work remains P-001 through P-004.\n- **P-007** `dropped` Create polished visual mockups grounded in the existing Sidestage interface blocked-by: P-001, P-002 importance: high — note: Duplicate entries created after multi-ptool output was not surfaced; canonical work remains P-001 through P-004.\n- **P-008** `dropped` Validate the mockups and deliver findings with implementation guidance blocked-by: P-003 importance: high — note: Duplicate entries created after multi-ptool output was not surfaced; canonical work remains P-001 through P-004.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n## Decisions\n\n(Use plans:add-decision to append. Each decision is a third-level\nheading with a date line and a body paragraph.)\n\n### D-001 — Separate event lifecycle activation from publisher media start\nDate: 2026-08-15\nCORRECTION (2026-08-15): The earlier decision incorrectly placed a merely scheduled event inside Active Event. That assumption is retracted; mockup #4 is rejected. Active Event remains a strict representation of the event currently running. If no event is running, it shows the existing no-active-event state; it must not mount a future event's Live Console. A scheduled event appears before activation in Event Manager and in the global Up Next rail, both with an explicit localized date, time, and time zone. If another event is currently active, that event remains unchanged in Active Event while the scheduled one remains visible only in those upcoming-event surfaces. At the scheduled instant, the server transitions the scheduled event to active; only then does it become the content of Active Event. Event Manager remains the authoritative lifecycle surface for a selected event: drafts expose primary `Start now` and secondary `Schedule event` actions. `Start now` confirms that the event becomes buyer-facing but does not start camera or microphone; media start remains the separate Live Console action. `Schedule event` uses accessible date, time, and time-zone fields and rejects past times. Reuse Sidestage's shipped primary/secondary actions, badge, card, and input patterns.\n",
