          "body": "Date: 2026-08-15\nDate: 2026-08-15\nThe encrypted SIDESTAGE_DEEPGRAM_API_KEY was replaced with Avi's approved grant-capable credential. Two secret-safe proofs now establish functional authorization without exposing the permanent key: (1) staging capability:bash.integration_env obtained POST /v1/auth/grant HTTP 200, opened the Listen WebSocket with the bearer subprotocol, streamed synthesized Opus audio, and received the known phrase as a final transcript; (2) the running production API container independently obtained HTTP 200 and a token from /v1/auth/grant. A byte-equivalent comparison also proves /opt/SideStage/.env.production already matches the replacement registry value; its mtime and the current container start predate the registry replacement, so production already held the working key and the encrypted registry was the stale location. This supersedes D-008's credential-absence snapshot and D-009's 403 condition for the credential wall only. P-014 resumes wip, but remains unshippable until current-tree full checks/builds and web-bundle secret scan pass, Papercusp bridge 5369b83c3 has exact green/deployed lineage, the guarded SideStage revision deploys, and a fresh public seller-to-buyer transcript readback is clean. Never record or expose the permanent key value.\nRelated: P-014",
