      "markdown": "---\ntitle: SideStage Watch — Coming up next mockup gallery\nslug: sidestage-watch-coming-up-next-mockups-2026-08-14\nstatus: ready\ncreated: 2026-08-15\nupdated: 2026-08-15\n---\n\n## Now\n\n**State:** Complete. D-003 records Avi’s selection of Concept 02 — Drop Runway. The standalone comparison gallery now annotates that choice in the toolbar, Concept 02 card, and footer; all three UI IR specs remain schema-valid and lint-clean with zero errors/warnings, and fresh desktop/mobile Verdict QA confirmed the accessible selection state, HTTP 200 responses, and no console messages. The owner-local review URL is http://127.0.0.1:41033/; canonical source remains design/sidestage-watch-coming-up-next-mockups-2026-08-14/index.html. No production SideStage UI was changed by this plan.\n\n**Next:** The separately approved Drop Runway production implementation may use D-003 and the canonical gallery as its design basis; this mockup-only plan needs no further edits.\n\n## Background\n\nThe current Watch tab renders Next in the drop as a conventional three-card product rail. This plan produces design mockups only; it does not modify production SideStage UI. The work is explicitly separate from the adjacent live-auction-module mockup plan and from the real-event-lineup data implementation.\n\nRequirements:\n- Preserve the existing SideStage cream/red/yellow visual language and real product-card information architecture.\n- Improve sequence clarity, anticipation, browseability, and the relationship between the immediate next item and later items.\n- Provide three materially different responsive directions side by side.\n- Use the Papercusp design-phase registry-first flow and validate/lint each UI specification.\n- Publish a comparison URL and verify it resolves and renders at desktop and mobile widths.\n\n## Phase 1 — Design\n\n- **P-001** `done` Search the react-tailwind design registry, inspect relevant reusable components, and define three responsive Coming up / Next in the drop directions as validated and linted UI specifications. importance: high — note: ← WI-39167 completed (done)\n\n## Phase 2 — Gallery\n\n- **P-002** `done` Build a polished side-by-side HTML comparison gallery using the verified SideStage brand and realistic product data. blocked-by: P-001 importance: high — note: ← WI-39170 completed (done)\n- **P-003** `done` Run browser verification at desktop and mobile widths; fix layout, console, and accessibility issues found in the gallery. blocked-by: P-002 importance: high — note: ← WI-39180 completed (done)\n- **P-004** `done` Publish the gallery, re-resolve the URL independently, and hand the verified link to Avi with a concise concept summary. blocked-by: P-003 importance: high — note: ← WI-39182 completed (done)\n\n## Decisions\n\n### D-001 — Mockup-only scope\n\nThis plan creates a review artifact and does not edit production SideStage components. Production implementation begins only after Avi chooses a direction.\n\n### D-002 — Separate from adjacent Watch work\n\nThe concurrent live-auction mockup plan targets bidding interactions; the event-lineup plan targets data authority; the completed page-audit plan covered whole-page redesign. This plan targets only the Coming up / Next in the drop product queue and may proceed independently.\n\n### D-003 — Avi selects Concept 02 — Drop Runway\nDate: 2026-08-15\nAvi selected Concept 02, Drop Runway, as the design direction on 2026-08-14. Treat it as the chosen basis for the subsequent production Watch-tab implementation; the current mockup/publishing plan remains scoped to gallery delivery until implementation is separately approved.\n",
