          "title": "Owner directive: WebSocket sync everywhere via shared @papercusp/sync on Rocicorp Zero",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\n[owner:Avi 2026-08-16 ET, interactive, verbatim] \"I read the architecture page and don't see anything about websockets, we were supposed to integrate websockets using the support we built for that into our shared sync library built on top of robicorp zero, I wanted to use websocket sync like everywhere in our app, is it being used? If not write a plan for implementing that, and updating relevant parts of our docs, architecture page, and our submission docs.\" (\"robicorp\" = Rocicorp.) Finding: WS is NOT in use — libs/sync carries a dormant Zero WebSocketAdapter + fallback machinery; apps/web/src/main.tsx:27 hardcodes syncType=\"SSE\"; no zero-cache exists server-side. This plan is the requested implementation + docs plan. Execution window (pre- vs post-submission cutover) remains an OPEN owner decision — see ## Now.\nRelated: P-001, P-004",
