          "id": "D-003",
          "title": "D-001 — Owner started execution; P-002/P-003 unblocked from P-001 and run in parallel",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\n**Authorization.** [owner:Avi 2026-08-16 ET, verbatim via fleet kickoff]: \"Are you or someone else working on getting the websockets based on our shared sync zero implementation working? if not, spin up an opus 5 xhigh agent to work on this. You can look at our restart project to see how we implemented it there.\" This supersedes the plan's wait-for-owner-review gate. Execution window = NOW. Route = a dedicated agent (su-68032) in fleet `sidestage-release-drive`.\n\n**Re-sequencing (AUTO-mode call, disclosed).** The plan chained P-002..P-008 behind P-001. That dependency is WRONG for P-002 and P-003, and holding it serialises the whole cutover behind the largest item.\n\nEvidence for the re-sequence, read from the tree (not assumed):\n- Zero replicates POSTGRES TABLES. Every table the contract package needs already exists in `db/schema.sql` (36 tables incl. `chat_message`, `auction_state`, `cart`, `checkout_order`, `event`, `event_config`, `event_lineup_item`, `event_run_of_show`, `copilot_proposal`, `storefront_product`, `product_catalog`). So the Zero schema/query/mutator package (P-002) can be authored and parity-tested today.\n- zero-cache provisioning (P-003) is infra — logical replication, publication, slot, Traefik WS routing. It depends on the tables existing, not on which process writes them.\n- P-001's REAL remaining scope is narrower than its text implies. `apps/api/src/db/` already ships pg stores for action-audit, action-item, auction-inventory, auction, cart, chat, event, order, scout-memory, scout-session, behind a `DATA_BACKEND=auto|pg|memory` switch (`database.module.ts`). The census's remaining \"memory backend authority\" rows are FOUR services: `config/event-config.service.ts` (configs), `copilot/copilot.store.ts` (proposals), `policies/policy.service.ts` (revisions + idem), `run-of-show/run-of-show.service.ts` (plans). Their tables (`event_config`, `copilot_proposal`, `seller_policy_revision`, `policy_idempotency`, `event_run_of_show`) already exist in schema.sql — the gap is pg store implementations, not migrations.\n\n**Therefore:** P-002 and P-003 are unblocked and proceed in parallel with P-001. P-004 (app root flip) keeps its real gate — it needs P-002 + P-003 landed AND P-001's four remaining pg stores done, because a Zero-replicated `event_config`/`copilot_proposal`/`seller_policy_revision`/`event_run_of_show` would read EMPTY while the API still holds those in process memory. That is the correctness dependency the original chain was reaching for; it belongs on P-004, not on P-002/P-003.\n\n**Reference implementation** (owner-named): `/home/marsh-office/Restart` — `libs/zero/{schema,queries,mutators}.ts` (@papercusp/zero contract package), `apps/shop-api/src/zero/zero.controller.ts` (`/zero/query` + `/zero/mutate` via `handleQueryRequest`/`handleMutateRequest`/`zeroPostgresJS`), `infra/zero/docker-compose.zero-us.yml` + `bin/zero-cache-start.sh` (zero-cache ops, incl. the 12GB-heap and stale-replica-lock lessons).\n\n**Version note:** `@rocicorp/zero` is declared `^1.3.0` in apps/web but the installed tree resolves **1.8.0**. Client/server/zero-cache image must be pinned to the SAME version at P-003 (Restart's plan calls this out and it is a known Zero footgun).\nRelated: P-001, P-002, P-003, P-004",
