          "id": "D-004",
          "title": "RETRACTED (wrong-tree audit): the \"no WebSocket transport\" re-scope is void — sidestage libs/sync HAS the Zero WS adapter; P-004 proceeds as originally scoped",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\n⚠ RETRACTED 07:20Z by the leader who issued it — the ruling below rested on a WRONG-TREE AUDIT and is void. The stop-gate on P-004 is LIFTED; the WI-39636→WI-39634 blocker edge is removed; P-004 is gated on P-001 only.\n\nWHAT ACTUALLY HOLDS (leader-verified 07:19Z against the tree apps/web RESOLVES, not the tree that was audited): sidestage's node_modules/@papercusp/sync is a symlink to ../../libs/sync — the SIDESTAGE tree's own copy — and that copy fully supports the flip: syncType DEFAULTS to 'WEBSOCKETS' (SyncProvider.tsx:202), schema/queries/mutators are destructured and consumed (:209-214, :281), a real WEBSOCKETS render path exists with a health-probe + PendingSyncAdapter gate (:306), and transports/websocket/WebSocketAdapter.tsx is built on @rocicorp/zero (Zero + ZeroProvider). P-004 as written is EXECUTABLE.\n\nTHE ERROR MECHANISM, recorded so it is not repeated: WI-39636 audited libs/generic/sync in the PAPERCUSP tree (where the WS adapter was genuinely removed in Z-2 and syncType='WEBSOCKETS' does silently render polling). The leader's \"independent verification\" read the SAME wrong tree — it shared the reporter's unstated resolution premise, so it corroborated recall, not fact. The decisive check was `readlink node_modules/@papercusp/sync` in the consumer's tree — run it BEFORE auditing any shared-package claim. Credit: su-bb5ea5f0 caught the premise within minutes.\n\nSURVIVING RESIDUE (real, but not this plan's): the papercusp-tree libs/generic/sync accepting syncType='WEBSOCKETS' and silently rendering POLLING with never-destructured schema/queries/mutators is a genuine latent API-contract trap THERE. WI-39636 is to be re-scoped to the papercusp harness at reduced severity (nothing in papercusp selects WEBSOCKETS today) — its regression-test idea (a requested-but-unavailable transport must fail loudly, never silently degrade) is worth landing in that library.",
