          "id": "D-006",
          "title": "WS \"live\" claims gate on SERVING evidence, not the main.tsx literal; docs DONE at truthful-at-every-instant wording; serving gap and gate-leg wiring become P-009/P-010",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\nFacts (verified 08:00-08:07Z; 659a7's finding msg mswy1o6s, mechanism corrected by bb5ea msg mswy85ga, leader-corroborated): P-004 flip LANDED (ebb028b, main.tsx syncType=\"WEBSOCKETS\"); flip-verify GREEN at unit level (web 734/734, deploy 90/90, typecheck 0, libs/sync 15/15; dispatch test mutation-verified — WI-39634 comment 69341). BUT WebSocket sync serves NOWHERE: the client dials the zero-cache origin directly (main.tsx:27 resolveZeroServerUrl → catalog.ts:76-81: VITE_ZERO_URL / dev localhost:4848 / prod ${origin}/zero; probeWebSocketOnce steps down to SSE on 'blocked') and nothing is listening at that origin anywhere (R1); separately the API /zero/query + /zero/mutate handlers zero-cache calls back into do not exist (R2). The app is healthy on SSE. The client NEVER calls /api/zero/* — their absence is not the step-down cause.\n\nRULINGS:\n1. Any doc/UI claim \"WebSocket sync is live\" gates on the SERVING bar: (a) zero-cache up + reachable at the origin the client resolves, on the instance the docs describe; (b) the /zero/query + /zero/mutate API handlers exist and answer (this app's P-002 contract design routes synced queries/custom mutators through them); (c) a client session actually holds a WS connection rather than falling back. A gate that greps the main.tsx literal is invalid.\n2. Docs lanes P-006/P-007/P-008: the D-005 flip-verify gate is CONFIRMED at unit level. DONE is allowed with truthful-at-every-instant wording — per P-008's own item text: \"SSE is live today and Zero WS is built and staged.\" No aspirational WS-live claims (D-002). Serving (P-011) is NOT a gate on the docs lanes (bb5ea's recommendation, adopted).\n3. P-008 scope: docs/PRD.md needs NO sync/data-plane change — 659a7's evidenced no-change accepted.\n4. R1/R2 attribution (bb5ea's archaeology, accepted): the handlers are P-002's item text verbatim (P-002 done ← WI-39605 WITHOUT them); prod zero-cache provisioning is P-003's lane (P-003 done ← WI-39616 with prod unapplied). Both are \"closed done, deliverable partially unshipped.\" The harness.ts:27/:127 + surfaces.ts:113 comments attributing the handlers to P-004 CONTRADICT the plan text and are drift — whoever does R2 corrects them in the same change. P-004 stays client-scoped; its completion claims no server work.\n5. LEADER ANSWER to bb5ea's filing question: R1+R2 are FILED as P-011 (this plan, Phase 2) — the plan item is the filing; no separate bare work-items needed (the WI materializes on claim, dodging the admission fence). bb5ea has first pick AFTER WI-39634's review-hold clears; evidence from mswy85ga attaches on claim. P-011 is required for the WS-live claim, NOT for submission-readiness (SSE serves).\n6. Gate coverage: libs/sync tests execute in NO sidestage gate leg (vitest.config.mts: three projects — deploy, api, web; libs/sync runs only via npm run test --workspace @papercusp/sync). P-012: wire libs/sync into the gate legs + prove with a deliberate red. Ship claim requires P-012 done.\n7. Production-surface question (7c55c): TDD.md ## Deployment STANDS. The SSEAdapter.tsx header \"The webapp is not the production user surface — see /CLAUDE.md\" is BORROWED papercusp text (cites a /CLAUDE.md absent from the entire sidestage tree + an apps/operator path). For SideStage, sidestage.papercusp.com IS the production user surface (live-verified 04:24Z; the submission sends reviewers there), alongside mobile v1.0.0. 7c55c takes the header correction.\n8. bb5ea's secondary finding (useTransportFallback fallbackTimer debounce swallows SSE's first onTransportError) is real — fix/verification folds into P-011 acceptance.\n\nRelated: P-004, P-006, P-007, P-008, P-011, P-012",
