          "id": "D-008",
          "title": "D-007 companion: unmeasured invariant (-1 detector-absent) must read UNKNOWN, not breach — authorized now, owner aa261, desktop-perf-gate.ts only",
          "body": "Date: 2026-08-17\nExecutes D-007 point 5 concurrently rather than deferring it. aa261's causal proof (msg mswzrhfn): harness_shared.desktop_perf_runs has NO harness scoping column; every run through 2026-08-16 22:42Z recorded webview-http-egress value=0 ok=true; the single 06:42:35Z run (perfrun-1786948955936-1bq7l7) recorded value=-1 ok=false — the DETECTOR-ABSENT sentinel per libs/generic/desktop-ipc/src/desktop-bootstrap.ts:181-185, which warns verbatim against exactly this conflation. desktop-perf-gate.ts:293 convicts (invariant && !ok) without checking the measure was taken, on a branch (:386) exempt from block-mode AND the PSI quiet-window. That one row froze promotion workspace-wide. D-007's no-desktop-app skip cures sidestage but NOT papercusp (which declares a desktop app and hits the same block the moment its tests green, with nobody looking).\n\nRULING [leader ratification of aa261's proposal, 08:50Z]: (1) aa261 lands the unmeasured-invariant fix NOW in desktop-perf-gate.ts ONLY — value=-1 (unmeasured) → verdictStatus 'unknown' + LOUD warn, mirroring the existing staleness branch (:374-378, \"nothing is measuring this ≠ the invariant is broken now\"); value>0 still blocks (real breach); value=0 still passes. NOT fail-open. (2) The 'unknown' path must ALERT/surface loudly enough that a permanently-absent detector gets noticed and filed — the alert replaces the (wrong) block as the safety valve; silent-skip is refused. (3) Falsifiability tests required: -1 → unknown+warn (no block, no silent pass); >0 → block; 0 → pass; and a guard against the >=0 careless-comparison class the bootstrap file warns about. (4) File separately, do not fix here: WHY the 06:42Z probe went unmeasurable (aa261's open undetermined — detector absent vs HTTP fallback vs probe crash). (5) No collision by construction: aa261 touches desktop-perf-gate.ts only; 659a7's D-007 skip (WI-39672) is in green-checkpoint.ts, queued behind d8292's WI-39450 lock; d8292 owns green-checkpoint.ts edits. (6) Landing order independent; EITHER fix unfreezes sidestage; both land regardless (skip = correct harness semantics, unknown = correct invariant semantics). (7) aa261's WI-39665 close condition unchanged: observed sidestage promotion (GATE_PROMOTION trailer promoted=true), citing whichever fix(es) landed.",
